$\mathrm{PCl}_5$ on reaction with alcohol and carboxylic acid, replace $-\mathrm{OH}$ group with $-\mathrm{Cl}$.

\begin{aligned}
\mathrm{ROH}+\mathrm{PCl}_5 \longrightarrow \mathrm{RCl} & +\mathrm{POCl}_3+\mathrm{HCl} \\
\mathrm{RCOOH}+\mathrm{PCl}_5 \longrightarrow & \mathrm{RCOCl}^2 \\
+ & \mathrm{POCl}_3+\mathrm{HCl}
\end{aligned}

Related Theory
$\mathrm{PCl}_5$ is used as a chlorinating agent and dehydrating agent for the synthesis of pesticides, phosphite antioxidants, plasticizers and stabilizers for plastic and elastomers etc

Acidic strength order \(\mathrm{HCO}_2 \mathrm{H}\gt \mathrm{C}_6 \mathrm{H}_5 \mathrm{CO}_2 \mathrm{H}\)
\(\therefore \mathrm{K}_{\mathrm{a}}\) order \(\mathrm{HCO}_2 \mathrm{H}\gt \mathrm{C}_6 \mathrm{H}_5 \mathrm{CO}_2 \mathrm{H} \quad\) {But \(\mathrm{C}_6 \mathrm{H}_5\) - group shows +I & +R effect}
So, \(\mathrm{pK}_{\mathrm{a}}\) order \(\mathrm{HCO}_2 \mathrm{H} \lt  \mathrm{C}_6 \mathrm{H}_5 \mathrm{CO}_2 \mathrm{H}\)

